% Font-map fallbacks for the wasm engine (appended by the dev server to every
% `<engine>/11/<name>.map` answer — pdfTeX honours the last entry, so these
% win over the map the cache was warmed with).
%
% Why: the TeX Live that warmed the cache has no cm-super, and this wasm
% engine has no mktexpk and no reachable mirror to rasterize with — every
% bitmap-only CM font dies with "bad pk file, expected pre" as soon as it
% ships (arXiv 2303.12712 hits cmttb10 on its first bold typewriter keyword
% inside a minted listing). Map each to the closest cached Type 1, reusing
% encoding vectors the base map already defines (CMTT12, CMMI10, CMBX10 are
% defined above line 4100 of the cached map, and we are appended after it).
% The pfb targets below (cmtt12, cmmi10, cmbx10) are verified present in the
% texlive-cache volume; unverified targets would 301 and fail noisily.

% bold typewriter — bitmap-only without cm-super
cmttb8 CMTT12 <cmtt12.pfb
cmttb9 CMTT12 <cmtt12.pfb
cmttb10 CMTT12 <cmtt12.pfb
cmttb12 CMTT12 <cmtt12.pfb
% light typewriter and sans typewriter — likewise bitmap-only
cmtl9 CMTT12 <cmtt12.pfb
cmtl10 CMTT12 <cmtt12.pfb
cmtss8 CMTT12 <cmtt12.pfb
cmtss9 CMTT12 <cmtt12.pfb
cmtss10 CMTT12 <cmtt12.pfb
% bold math italic — bitmap-only; slanted bold — upright approximation
cmmib8 CMMI10 <cmmi10.pfb
cmmib9 CMMI10 <cmmi10.pfb
cmmib10 CMMI10 <cmmi10.pfb
cmbxsl10 CMBX10 <cmbx10.pfb
% typewriter sizes whose own pfb is not in the cache either — the base map
% points cmtt8/cmtt9 at cmtt10.pfb and cmtt10 at its own missing pfb; every
% one of those 301s. Route all cached tt sizes at the cached cmtt12.pfb.
cmtt8 CMTT12 <cmtt12.pfb
cmtt9 CMTT12 <cmtt12.pfb
cmtt10 CMTT12 <cmtt12.pfb
